{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QUm3kTwDxVrs2M5AFojp4e","type":"tool_result","content":"206:\tDrainMS    int       `json:\"drain_ms,omitempty\"`\n235:\t// drain deadline and the ones that did not.\n236:\tDrained   int64 `json:\"drained,omitempty\"`\n237:\tAbandoned int64 `json:\"abandoned,omitempty\"`\n259:\t// Busy, when set, counts work a handler left running after it answered (a command whose\n260:\t// deadline passed): it is in flight for the idle timeout, the drain and the status.\n261:\tBusy func() int64\n336:\tinflight atomic.Int64\n365:\t\ts.inflight.Add(1)\n369:\t\t\tdefer s.inflight.Add(-1)\n385:\t\t\tif s.inflight.Load()+s.busy() == 0 && time.Since(time.Unix(0, atomic.LoadInt64(&s.last))) >= s.opts.Idle {\n434:\t\tdrain := defaultDrain\n436:\t\t\tdrain = time.Duration(req.DrainMS) * time.Millisecond\n438:\t\t// No new connection is accepted while the requests in flight drain.\n440:\t\t// The reply of a long drain must still be writable.\n441:\t\t_ = conn.SetDeadline(time.Now().Add(drain + requestDeadline))\n442:\t\treply := s.drain(drain)\n470:// drain waits, up to the deadline, for the requests in flight besides this one.\n471:func (s *server) drain(deadline time.Duration) Reply {\n472:\tbefore := s.inflight.Load() + s.busy() - 1\n474:\tfor s.inflight.Load()+s.busy() > 1 && time.Now().Before(end) {\n477:\tleft := s.inflight.Load() + s.busy() - 1\n489:func (s *server) busy() int64 {\n490:\tif s.opts.Busy == nil {\n493:\treturn s.opts.Busy()\n503:\t\tUptimeMS: time.Since(s.started).Milliseconds(), IdleMS: s.opts.Idle.Milliseconds(), InFlight: s.inflight.Load() + s.busy() - 1, Served: s.served.Load()}\n651:// Stop asks the runtime to drain within the deadline and exit.\n652:func (c Client) Stop(ctx context.Context, drain time.Duration) (Reply, error) {\n653:\treturn c.roundTrip(ctx, Request{Op: \"stop\", DrainMS: int(drain.Milliseconds())})"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"f267