k up that it ran in the runtime.\n  - Its output is still never compared, and nothing checks it.\n- **N5 (low)** at `pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:161`: when a deadline passes, `busy` goes up before the handler returns. The connection only stops counting as in flight after the reply is written and closed (`runtime.go:369`).\n  - In that short window, one command is counted twice. A status in that window shows `InFlight` one too high, and a stop counts the command as drained when it is really still running.\n  - Commit dd02ad63 changed the stop-count test to tolerate this window rather than removing it.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_measure_test.go\", \"line\": 280, \"summary\": \"The heavy check run alongside the short queries discards its output and via, yet the T5 verdict (:378) claims every hosted run printed the standalone output; lane metrics corroborate it ran hosted, but its output is never compared.\", \"action\": \"Compare the concurrent heavy run's output and via with the standalone run before T5 passes, as S6 does.\", \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go\", \"line\": 161, \"summary\": \"At a deadline busy is incremented before the handler returns, while the connection stays in inflight until the reply is written and closed (runtime.go:369); in that window one command counts twice, so status InFlight can read one too high and a stop overcounts drained.\", \"action\": \"Increment busy after the connection leaves inflight (or count the deadline handoff atomically), and make the stop-count test strict again.\", \"owner\": \"pose-mcp maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-10\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:49,53-58 and .json:395-411 record CPU ms, peak and end RSS per scenario and two simultaneous heavy checks (T7); harness runtime_measure_test.go:230-311.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/worktreeruntime/runtime.go:472-483: before and left both use inflight+busy-1, both clamped at 0; test runtime_test.go:467.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"Report (:3,:10,:49,:53-58) and JSON fourth run carry T7, per-scenario CPU and peak RSS; T7 is in R8 at .pose/specs/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-qos-and-measurement.md:43 with its late addition disclosed; ADR :302-304 now matches.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N2\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:126-133,160-162: busy only after the caller's deadline via the orphaned CAS state; test runtime_host_test.go:287 asserts InFlight==1 for a running command with its caller waiting. Residual transient window reported as N5.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R2-N3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"runtime_measure_test.go:50-57 reads getconf CLK_TCK; :59-74,:240 reset and read VmHWM per scenario via clear_refs; :277 keeps short_idle CPU (JSON cpu_ms_short_idle, peak_rss_mib_short_idle).\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Read in full: the measurement report and its JSON (all four runs), runtime_measure_test.go, worktreeruntime/runtime.go (server, handle, drain, state), cli/runtime_host.go (hosted handler, lanes admission, deadline handoff), pose/resident_git_memo.go, and the memo integration in governance_read_view_git.go (key, store-only-when-pure, --no-replace-objects). Also read the roadmap milestone and exit gate, the ADR B35 amendments, the qos spec R8, the member specs' status and unchecked tasks, and the named regression tests. No shell was available in this run (Bash denied), so no tests or plan tools were executed; regression relies on the sealed evidence.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"exit-gate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the exit gate (roadmap :74-78) against the code and the fourth measurement run: field-by-field handshake and per-request identity (runtime.go:426,449-455), peer credentials before read (:404-408), restart inherits nothing (T2), standalone fallback (T6), memo keyed by commit/shallow/config with no watcher, no rerun of possibly-run commands, short-query QoS and deterministic output under one and two heavy jobs (T3,T5,T7) with RAM/CPU/latency per scenario. CPU quota and per-command limits are not delivered and are disclosed in ADR :299-304; concluded the gate has falsifiable evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The ADR amendment of 2026-11-10 composes the three slices (endpoint/handshake, hosted checks with resident memo, admission lanes); the hosted handler uses the server's identity check, the lanes and the memo without contradiction; the sealed integration evidence of all three member specs passes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"membership\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"All three ordered member specs show status: done and have no unchecked task (searched ^- \\\\[ \\\\]); the last commit carries the three member specs.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"regression\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the sealed cumulative module validation: build, unit and the full integration/reachability set for pose-mcp all pass. Not re-run here because the shell was denied.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Cross-spec departures (no watcher, no CPU quota or per-command limits, Windows standalone, B33 views not reused) are disposed in the ADR's final amendment; the remaining findings N4 and N5 are low and carry follow-ups with owner and date.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Relied on the sealed strict validation (commit 95acbc58 records it); the shell was denied in this run, so it was not re-executed by the reviewer.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it runs after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check milestone:pose-shared-runtime/optional-worktree-runtime\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it runs after the attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess discover --component pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the shell was denied in this run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose assess tech-debt\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the shell was denied in this run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended only; the shell was denied in this run.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nThe required `validate` tool is marked `passed` using the sealed `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` result, and the rationale says I didn't re-run it. If POSE requires a `command:` I actually ran for that tool, it will refuse the draft. In that case, allow `pose validate` in this profile and run the review again.","ttft_ms":1277,"type":"result","duration_ms":117089,"uuid":"a0ed669f-17a7-44bd-8780-77b3a2fa09ce","ttft_stream_ms":809,"time_to_request_ms":49,"first_content_frame_ms":809,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":12564,"cacheReadInputTokens":620513,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48177,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7609426,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3810,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":48177,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
